    "created_at": "2026-05-12T13:09:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-12T13:26:35Z",
    "body": "If things go wacky in VS Code regarding missing Activity Bar icons and their associated panels, press `SHIFT + CTRL + P` (or Mac equivalent) for VS Code Command Bar and type **reset view** to bring up VS Code's `Reset View Locations` command and press Enter. This should restore any custom changes you made to UI layout.\n\nTo restore the VS Code Continue key bind you have to head to `Manage -> Keyboard Shortcuts`, type Continue in the search bar and look for `Continue: Add to Chat` or maybe `Continue: Focus Continue Chat` and check the active key binds there and, if empty, add your own.\n\nAll extension icons in the Activity Bar open their panels adjacent to the Activity Bar by default (`Explorer`, `Search`, `Run & Debug`, `Source Control` etc) and dragging the panel name to the right side is equivalent to dragging the icon from the Activity Bar itself over to the right. The icon will disappear as the panel is opened on the right. To get the icon back, drag the Continue panel from the right side and drop it on the Activity Bar at your chosen position.\n\nThis is a quirk of Activity Bar icons always opening their panels adjacent to the Activity Bar and there's no way to specify panel position left or right independently of the Activity Bar position.\n\nThe only other drastic option to get things on the right is to go to `View -> Appearance -> Move Primary Side Bar Right`, but I suspect that's not what people here want.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
